Below is the change description:
To expand the persistence options for Spring AI's chat memory beyond existing solutions (like JDBC, MongoDB, Redis, and Neo4j), enabling developers to leverage scalable and cost-effective cloud-native storage via Amazon S3 or S3-compatible services like MinIO.
Introduced a new S3-based implementation for the ChatMemoryRepository, including its core implementation (S3ChatMemoryRepository), auto-configuration (S3ChatMemoryAutoConfiguration), configuration properties, and a dedicated Spring Boot starter. Added support for S3 bucket operations, JSON-based message serialization, and integration tests using LocalStack.

